        "description": {
          "value": "<p>When the [[lookup @name lowercase]] hasn’t spit its Acid Breath, the acid built up within the [[lookup @name lowercase]] causes the patina on its scales to spread to weapons that strike it. While the [[lookup @name lowercase]]'s Acid Breath is available, any weapon made of metal that hits the [[lookup @name lowercase]] corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If a nonmagical weapon’s penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal that hits the [[lookup @name lowercase]] is destroyed after dealing damage. A magical weapon can’t have a penalty greater than −5, and a magical weapon removes this penalty after 24 hours or after its attuned wielder finishes a long rest.</p>",
